1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
 Thank you very much for the question. In fact, I will answer exactly the same answer that I answered the last week.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:15,000
 You know, we as a city of Montreal, and the STM, we are extremely sensitive to the situation of people with reduced mobility.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
 We have certainly had a program for the STM, financed by the government of Quebec in 2016,

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
 and we have succeeded, since 2016, to make 20 stations accessible.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,200
 I would also like to remember that 96% of our buses have already a ramp accessible, so we make our buses also accessible.

6
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:42,760
 The problem we have now is that the funding to make the stations accessible is not there, not at the rendezvous,

7
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:49,400
 and there will certainly be representations that will be made auprès of the government who was named here.

8
00:00:49,400 --> 00:01:02,200
 And we will certainly proceed, or will try to make this issue an important issue for people with reduced mobility and to make the stations of the STM even more accessible.

9
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:09,000
 I would like to remind you, before finishing, that we have currently 31 stations of the STM accessible. Thank you.

10
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
 Thank you, Mr. Salem.

11
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:19,000
 Second question, Mr. David Gamper, l'Association des Piétons et Cyclistes de NDJ.

12
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:29,000
 On Terrebonne Street, in CDN-NDG, a one-way street, the borough proposes for this coming winter

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:40,000
 to remove one of the two protected cycle lanes and have cyclists in that direction ride in a single traffic lane

14
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:52,000
 3.5 meters wide between two rows of parked cars. The minimum separation of one meter required to

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:02,720
 pass a cyclist is not available and this forces either unsafe overtaking or cars to drive being

16
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:12,380
 cyclists at their speed. Moreover, in snow and high conditions, unclear edges often force

17
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:21,920
 cyclists to ride further out into the road, making it even more dangerous for cars to

18
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:32,300
 overtake. My question is, has the SPVM been consulted on this layout and what is their

19
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:37,080
 opinion, will they carry out increased surveillance?

20
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:42,000
 Monsieur Alexandre Toyderesco.

21
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:43,780
 Merci, Monsieur le Président.

22
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:45,440
 Thank you for the question, Mr. Gamper.

23
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:50,040
 We have to start by acknowledging that many residents felt that their concerns regarding

24
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:53,880
 the Terrebonne bike path were not heard by the previous administration.

25
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:58,800
 We heard this message clearly, and we want to make, to have a different approach, not

26
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,820
 a dogmatic one, but a very pragmatic one.

27
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:05,540
 I know it's very difficult for some to understand our approach, but nevertheless, you will see it in action.

28
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:10,060
 Residents expect us to listen and to act, and this is exactly what we're doing.

29
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:14,680
 Our approach is simple, listen, act, evaluate the results, and adjust as needed.

30
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:21,420
 That is why we're introducing a new winter configuration on the Terrebonne bike path and testing it over the coming months.

31
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:27,940
 We will also consult residents to hear their feedback and better understand how this configuration responds to the needs of the neighborhood.

32
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:33,100
 And to make sure that our evaluation is based not only on feedback but also on objective data,

33
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:39,620
 I have asked that our new generation of traffic counters be deployed on Terrebonne Street starting this winter.

34
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:44,000
 This will help us better measure how the street is being used and the impact of the new configuration.

35
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:49,740
 Public safety is paramount in our endeavor to find the right balance.

36
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:57,660
 And I say this not only as an elected official but also as an avid cyclist and as the father of two young cyclists who use the bike path.

37
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:04,340
 Their safety matters deeply to me, just as the safety of everyone who uses the Terrebonne bike path.

38
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:07,920
 And we're not looking to impose a one-size-fits-all solution, Mr. President.

39
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:15,280
 We want to work with all residents to find the best possible balance between active mobility, road safety, and the residents' quality of life.

40
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:16,460
 Thank you very much.

41
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:19,220
 Merci, M. Théo de Rescot.

42
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:28,100
 Troisième question, je tiens à signaler que les questions en ligne, c'est toujours une question.

43
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:32,080
 Alors, dans la présente question, il y a deux questions.

44
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:35,680
 Donc, avec le greffier, on respecte les règlements.

45
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,940
 La deuxième question ne sera pas posée aujourd'hui.

46
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:41,380
 La question vient de Sue Stacho.

47
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,380
 Sauvons l'anse-à-l'homme.

48
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:44,400
 Hello.

49
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:54,060
 Recently, a wide swatch of land was cut and how planned life was raised to ground level

50
00:04:54,060 --> 00:05:05,160
 along the servitude previously known as the Empires 440 within the boundaries of the Grand

51
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:12,620
 Pacte de l'Ouest between Gouin Boulevard and Pierrefonds Boulevard. What is the nature

52
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:22,100
 of this work and is this preparation work for laying an urban boulevard or any type

53
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:31,140
 of road through this section of the park where privately hound lots are located?

54
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:35,380
 Who wants to answer this question?

55
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,460
 Mr. Bates?

56
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:39,600
 Pardon, Mr. President.

57
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,680
 Mrs. Stackwell, thank you very much for your question.

58
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:48,000
 In fact, the work that was done, let me just start by saying that that portion of land

59
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,260
 does not belong to us, it belongs to the Minister of Transport.

60
00:05:51,260 --> 00:06:07,820
 There has been some work, as you've stated, between Gouin and Pierrefonds Boulevard and that was essentially to reprofile the ditches to be able to naturally control the runoff water on the surface to get it to the river at the end of Gouin Boulevard.

61
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:25,420
 And as far as the work or potential work or announced work for the urban boulevard, we know that we are still working on the plan to have an accessible point from Antoine Faucon to get folks up to the REM as was described for the last number of years.

62
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:30,000
 We are still looking at some of those options on how we can integrate that in the natural space.

